{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1483579-fae-vehicles","id":1483579,"title":"Fae Vehicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-10T06:42:57-07:00","id":1483579,"title":"Fae Vehicles?","content":"So the Fae Mount merit applies to creatures, but what about fae vehicles? Things like a broomstick, or a morter/pestle, or maybe even a Faerie coach? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25281-coachman","name":"Coachman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T18:47:06-07:00","id":1483669,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Fae Chariot</b><br /> I gave this some thought today, and came up with two versions of the same basic idea. One is a merit, the other is a Contract. Try them out and see if they work for you. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fae Chariot (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> A Fae Chariot is a rarity; a Token that is also a means of transport. The appearance of a Fae Chariot can vary wildly; some appear as relatively mundane vehicles, while others take or the fantastical shapes flying brooms or pumpkin carriages. In the Hedge, the vehicle always appears parked in a convenient and accessible spot. Most fae chariots can\u2019t leave the Hedge, fading into nothing if they try and reforming somewhere inside the Hedge after a day and a night. Choose one of the following sets of traits;<br /> \u2022 Dice Modifier -1, Size 7, Durability 2, Structure 9, Speed 100. The Fae Chariot is similar to a motorcycle.<br /> \u2022 Dice Modifier -2, Size 10, Durability 3, Structure 13, Speed 90. The Fae Chariot is similar to a mid-sized car.<br /> \u2022 Dice Modifier -3, Size 15, Durability 3, Structure 18, Speed 80. The Fae Chariot is similar to a truck or van.<br /> Additionally, each dot of this Merit allows the vehicle one of the following special abilities:<br /> <i>Dream Machine:</i> The transformed vehicle, no matter how large or ungainly, maneuvers smoothly and easily. The vehicle\u2019s dice modifier is equal to the changelings Wyrd (maximum +5)<br /> <i>Goblin Mechanic:</i> The vehicle repairs itself. Once per Scene, as long as the vehicle has at least one box of Structure left, the changeling may spend a point of Glamour to remove all damage<br /> <i>Hedgewheel:</i> The vehicle\u2019s movement defies the limits of its design. Once per scene, it can either drive across water, move up buildings, or fly at it\u2019s normal speed for a number of turns equal to Wyrd+3 this Merit.<br /> <i>Street Legal:</i> Most Fae Chariots cannot manifest outside the Hedge. With Street Legal, the changeling can bring it through a gate into the mundane world, where it persists as long as the changeling fuels it a point of Glamour once per scene. Like your changeling, the vehicle has a Mask, which the character can scour away or reinforce just like his own.<br /> <i>Troll Tough:</i> The vehicle becomes fantastically resistant to damage. Add two to the vehicle\u2019s Durability. In addition to the increase to structure from Durability, add an additional [Wyrd] points to Structure.<br /> <i>Wyrd Engine:</i> The Wyrd empowers the vehicle with supernatural acceleration and speed. Add 20 to its Speed and the High Acceleration tag. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fae Chariot (Jewel \u2013 Royal)</b></span><br /> Tales of the few often depict unusual modes of transport. Changelings with this contract can transform relatively mundane objects into magical vehicles, of impart mundane vehicles with supernatural potency. While the contract is named for the myths of witches riding brooms, pumpkin carriages, fantastic dirigibles, or cars with super-charged goblin engines are all possible.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Crafts + Wyrd<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Success:</b> The changeling a transforms an object large enough to bear their weight into a conveyance. Most such objects are Size 4 or greater. The contract lasts until the end of the Scene. Objects without steering, wheels, legs, or similar attributes hover comfortably above the ground and respond to mental command. The object (if not already a vehicle), retain their Durability and structure and have following additional traits;<br /> <b>Size 4 -Size 8:</b> Such objects have the rough speed and maneuverability of a motorcycle. Dice Modifier -1, Speed 100<br /> <b>Size 9 -Size 15:</b> Such objects have the rough speed and maneuverability of a typical car. Dice Modifier -2, Speed 90<br /> <b>Size 16 -Size 20:</b> Such objects have the rough speed and maneuverability of a typical van. Dice Modifier -3, Speed 80<br /> In addition, the changeling may add one of the following features to the object. If the object is already a vehicle, add an additional feature.<br /> <i><b>Dream Machine:</b></i> The transformed vehicle, no matter how large or ungainly, maneuvers smoothly and easily. The vehicle\u2019s dice modifier is equal to the changelings Wyrd (maximum +5)<br /> <i><b>Godmother\u2019s Gift:</b></i> The changeling can alter the size, shape and appearance of the vehicle. This includes cosmetic features, such as accessories, coloring, and shape, but also allows objects as small as Size 1 be altered into vehicles, expanding to any size between 4 and 20. A compact car could be turned into a limousine, pumpkin might be turned into a carriage, or a toy truck might become a real one.<br /> <i><b>Goblin Mechanic:</b></i> The vehicle repairs itself. Once per Scene, as long as the vehicle has at least one box of Structure left, the changeling may spend a point of Glamour to remove all damage<br /> <i><b>Hedgewheel:</b></i> The vehicle\u2019s movement defies the limits of its design. Once per scene, it can either drive across water, move up buildings, or fly at it\u2019s normal speed for a number of turns equal to Wyrd+3 this Merit.<br /> <b><i>Troll Tough:</i> </b>The vehicle becomes fantastically resistant to damage. Add two to the vehicle\u2019s Durability. In addition to the increase to structure from Durability, add an additional [Wyrd] points to Structure.<br /> <i><b>Wyrd Engine:</b></i> The Wyrd empowers the vehicle with supernatural acceleration and speed. Add 20 to its Speed and the High Acceleration tag.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Add an additional feature.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Contract fails.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The object warps rather than transforms. This deals [Wyrd] points of damage to the object.<br /> <b>Loophole:</b> The vehicle has already been customized or modified by mundane means to suit the changeling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T22:37:51-07:00","id":1483692,"title":"","content":"So the short answer of the above is &quot;Yeah, they're Tokens usually.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}